WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.930
this is starting to sort of get repetitive.

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:02.930
I think it's still really

00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:03.930
important to do.

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:07.620
We have a cycle that has become very common
in modern American politics.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.660
The president makes a completely unrealistic
promise.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.940
He then fails to deliver on that promise.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:17.490
Then he brags about the results even though
they fall short of his promise.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:23.869
Then we find out he criticized a democratic,
uh, operative of politician or prior president

00:00:23.869 --> 00:00:26.000
for the exact same result.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:31.119
This time it's Barack Obama over the GDP and
Donald Trump's prediction of four or five

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:33.620
or even 6% GDP growth.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:36.170
Let me set it up for you and we'll get right
into it.

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:38.800
GDP is the gross domestic product.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.610
It's one of the main ways that we measure
the size of our economy.

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:46.719
There's a lot of debate over whether GDP is
the right way to evaluate an economy.

00:00:46.719 --> 00:00:51.590
But putting that aside for now, this is the
total value of all the stuff we produce in

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:53.899
the services that we provide in a year.

00:00:53.899 --> 00:00:55.390
That's our GDP.

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:59.149
During his campaign and after becoming president,
Donald Trump was talking about we're going

00:00:59.149 --> 00:01:05.570
to have 3% GDP growth, 4% GDP growth, five
even 6% GDP growth.

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:08.140
Here's just one example of Donald Trump doing
this.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:09.960
This one's during his presidency.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:13.080
He's been predicting it since he was just
candidate Trump.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:19.880
But to get going in a way, I really want where
we have GTP getting up to four or five and

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:21.490
even 6% because I think that's possible.

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:27.320
If you look back in your notes, you'll say,
when I said 4% uh, people said that would

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.320
be years.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.750
Well, it's turned out that I'm right because
without the hurricanes, this last quarter,

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:34.330
we would have hit 4%

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:36.360
so of course none of this has happened.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:41.840
And yesterday we learned that in the third
quarter of this year, the GDP was just 1.9%

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:44.970
now, just it's actually pretty normal.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:47.500
That's a relatively normal level of GDP growth.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:51.910
It's not particularly good or particularly
bad, but the thing is, Donald Trump is now

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:55.450
cheering it as if it is a signal of the best
economy ever.

00:01:55.450 --> 00:02:03.810
Literally tweeting yesterday, quote the greatest
economy in American history, but back in 2012

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:10.230
when Barack Obama had the exact same 1.9%
GDP growth, what did Donald Trump tweet?

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.440
Because there's a tweet for everything.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:20.380
Donald Trump tweeted, Q1 GDP has just been
revised down to 1.9% the economy is in deep

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:22.690
trouble, and of course it wasn't.

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:28.440
But if it was, then Trump's economy must likewise
be in deep trouble on the basis of those same

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:29.860
GDP numbers.

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:35.790
So this is one more of Donald Trump's insane
predictions and his distortions and his being

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:38.200
the pot that calls the kettle black.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.970
But this is also economically disastrous.

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:42.150
And I'm going to tell you why.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:48.740
Remember Donald Trump, when he told us about
his tax cut plan was told that's going to

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:49.990
blow up the deficit.

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:50.990
It doesn't balance.

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:52.710
It's going to explode the deficit.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:54.790
And Donald Trump said, no, no, no.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:58.890
This tax cut plan is going to cause such growth.

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:06.590
We're going to cause you know, 3% 4% 5% 6%
GDP growth that the growth will pay for the

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:11.850
tax cuts in a way that none of the analysts
are coming clean with you about.

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:17.530
The proposal for tax cuts was scored and it
was a train wreck, totally underwater, hugely

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:21.430
deficit exploding, but his acolytes repeated
this claim.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.260
They said the estimates are wrong.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:28.810
GDP will be up up, up five, 6% it'll pay for
the tax cuts in total.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:34.270
Now, aside from whether that makes sense at
all, and I would argue it doesn't, it's what

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:39.370
he claimed and it is not happening and his
followers are falling for it.

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:44.480
We were told the GDP will go up so much that
the tax cuts will be paid for and everything

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.010
is going to be so good.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:50.700
Everybody will win every just winning for
everybody and instead the opposite has happened

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:54.500
and we are now curating or maybe there's a
better way of saying it.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:04:01.770
Trumpism is curating one of the lowest information,
electorates that actually thrives on Trump

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:06.720
lies and is energized by the distortions,
which they can then go and repeat all over

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:12.069
the internet and Twitter and the normal enclaves
applying no critical analysis whatsoever either

00:04:12.069 --> 00:04:16.239
because they're choosing not to apply any
critical analysis or because they lack the

00:04:16.239 --> 00:04:20.970
intellectual capacity and knowledge of critical
thinking and epistemology that might be required

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:26.510
to do that analysis of what Donald Trump is
telling them, but it is hugely damaging to

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:27.790
the economy.

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:32.940
It's hugely damaging to the fabric of the
country in terms of just basic intellectual

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:38.430
rigor and thinking and it has opened the door
for this to become the absolute new norm.

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:39.940
Normal in future presidencies.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:42.980
In future campaigns where promises don't matter.

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:48.620
Any failed promise by the person on your quote
team is either because someone is misstating

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:53.350
what the promise was or because of the other
party that got in the way or because of where

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:55.930
the [inaudible] it doesn't even matter what
it is, will excuse it saying in some way,

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:57.070
shape or form.

00:04:57.070 --> 00:05:02.190
The left does this to some degree it's not
as bad, but I don't want to do it and if you

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:07.320
see me doing it then I hope you will call
me out for applying a different standard to

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:08.760
the left than than the right.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:15.180
One of my priorities and I think I'm doing
an okay job of it, is when the same criticism

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:16.690
could apply to both parties.

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:18.570
I apply it to both parties.

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:23.290
When there are differences between the parties,
I point out what they are and when the status

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:28.419
quo is either implicitly or explicitly reinforced
by both parties, uh, because it's more of

00:05:28.419 --> 00:05:31.130
an establishment versus anti-establishment
thing.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.150
I hope that I'm pointing that out to you as
well.

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:34.610
If I'm, if I'm falling short of that goal,
I do want you to let me know.

